The play program must, each time it runs: build a single BDL entry at r12 pointing at r7 with r10 frames worth of samples, program BDBAR (NABM+0x10), set LVI (NABM+0x15) to 0, set the run bit in the PCM-out control register (NABM+0x1B bit0), then poll until the DMA halts (status NABM+0x16 bit0 = DMA Controller Halted), then stop and halt.

AC'97 PCM-out box at NABM base 0xc400:
- 0x10 BDBAR (dword: physical address of BDL, 8-byte aligned)
- 0x14 CIV, 0x15 LVI (byte), 0x16 SR (word), 0x18 PICB (word), 0x1A PIV, 0x1B CR (byte)

BDL entry = 8 bytes: dword buffer physaddr, word length in SAMPLES (16-bit samples, not bytes), word control (bit15 IOC, bit14 BUP). Length is number of samples = frames * channels.
